Subject: vk: include vkutils/image.h in VKOverlays.h
Why: ui_overlay_renderer holds std::vector/map of std::unique_ptr<vk::image>
     and inherits a virtual destructor, so vk::image must be complete when
     the class is defined. The header only sees the forward declaration
     from vkutils/sync.h and relies on include-order luck; libc++ (NDK)
     rejects it (static_assert in unique_ptr's deleter), libstdc++ happens
     to accept. Include the definition directly.
Upstream-status: candidate

diff --git a/rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKOverlays.h b/rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKOverlays.h
index e354d23..3a6e89a 100644
--- a/rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKOverlays.h
+++ b/rpcs3/Emu/RSX/VK/VKOverlays.h
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 
 #include "vkutils/data_heap.h"
 #include "vkutils/descriptors.h"
+#include "vkutils/image.h"
 #include "vkutils/graphics_pipeline_state.hpp"
 
 #include "Emu/IdManager.h"
